  "body": "## Summary\n\nPR #2709 leaves the physical seek cost of QQ16 output-slice scratch access open. This source-bound package prices its two scalar sweeps and supplies one paid streaming variant.\n\n```text\nunchanged per-site word, bank-major: 8564*N^2 + 306*N - 2 steps\nunchanged per-site word, site-major: 9300*N - 432 steps\n24 extra unit ADDs, bank-major streaming: 11866*N - 2840 steps\n```\n\nEight scratch subtractions use an existing dirty Z0 output and restore it exactly. The variant needs no additional payload array in the declared word-address model. It raises the complete added local scalar allowance from 17,280 to 17,472 and requires exclusive W-bank ownership across each whole window. Native events remain unchanged.\n\nThe package includes a proof for every positive integer N, a pinned compressed source word, exact receipts, a standalone checker and registered replay. Credit ywz65/PR #2709 and #2540, commdata2338/PR #2651, and the retained QQ16 lineage. Direct source head is `d7749c49e967b214537c0bd832e435e177e21d4f`; exact pins and provenance are in `SOURCES.json` and `TASK.json`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** PR #2709's access contract leaves seeks and staging unpriced.\n  **After:** exact coefficients derived from the literal word, checked against address traces at N=1..32,64, with rational dirty-state and restoration controls at N=2,3,5.\n- CPython 3.12.15 registered normal/optimized replay and four artifact tests pass. Direct Python 3.14 checks and Ruff E/F/B/UP/SIM pass. Git-free read-only export, source/typed-receipt corruption and equivalent recompression are covered.\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/qq16-scratch-travel\n```\n\nPriority revision 5, task `joint-query-controller`; initial main `c3c94c2ea`, checked main `78ceed413`, relevant guidance/inputs unchanged. [Claim and handoff](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2617#discussioncomment-18955159). Complete overlap snapshots and limitations are recorded in TASK.json.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way.\n\n**Blast Radius:** isolated.\n\nOne new research package and its opt-in replay. No selected-frontier change. These are fixed-protocol address tariffs, not global schedule minima or a runtime/kappa improvement. Whole-window ownership/retention, bit arithmetic, instruction control, surrounding native placement and a complete caller remain open. No selected cold replay, native-kernel admission or Lean proof is claimed. New work is Apache-2.0.\n",
